  "policy": {
    "paths": "NFC, forward-slash separators; preserve this spelling in path. pathKey applies locale-independent lower -> upper -> lower -> NFC to path. Java must use Normalizer.normalize(path.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT).toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT), Normalizer.Form.NFC); never default-locale casing. This is a conservative collision rule, not full Unicode casefold. Sigma variants collide; sharp-S ẞ/ß/SS collide as ss. Dotted İ and i+combining-dot collide but remain distinct from plain I/i. Dotless ı conservatively collides with I/i. Keys must remain stable under normalization. Reject empty/dot segments, absolute paths, Windows forbidden characters, trailing dots/spaces and device names. Native ports must additionally check filesystem collisions, symlinks and junctions, including runtime Unicode-version differences.",
    "identity": "Distinct IDs never converge, even with identical bytes. Live distinct IDs with the same pathKey conflict as path-collision. The caller supplies candidates; planEntry cannot discover other entries.",
    "absence": "null means no known version, not a tombstone. Missing sides of a known base conflict; deletion requires an explicit tombstone.",
    "equality": "Compare ID, kind, NFC path with case preserved, hash, length and deleted; ignore opaque revisions and clocks. Tombstones retain path/kind for conservative comparison."
  },
